# Engineering code style

Match the file you are editing. This repo has no Prettier config and no
`import/order` ESLint rule. Do not invent a second format.

## TypeScript / React (`src`)

- Prefer 2-space indent; keep the file's existing quote style
- Comments: **中文注释为主**（仓库现状），跟随所在文件语言；与用户交流用**中文**
- **Relative imports only** — no path alias (`@/`, `@repo/*`, …); no `tsconfig` paths
- Keep `strict` + `verbatimModuleSyntax`; use `import type` for type-only imports
- Do not add `eslint-disable` unless the user asks
- Client env / native access: only through existing helpers (`src/storage`, `src/ai`, Tauri invoke guards). Do not invent `VITE_*` or `import.meta.env` usage
- UI copy: must go through `src/i18n` (`messages/zh.ts` + `messages/en.ts` as a pair) via `useI18n`; never hardcode user-facing strings
- UI styling: Tailwind 4 utilities against semantic tokens in `src/styles/main.css`; reuse `src/components/primitives.tsx` / `src/components/layout/AppShell.tsx`. Do not add antd, Radix/shadcn, ahooks, or styled-components

## Import grouping (when adding new files)

builtin → external (`react` first) → parent (`../../`) → sibling (`./`) → type imports

## Tests

Pure logic unit tests live in `tests/*.test.ts` and run with
`node --experimental-strip-types` (`npm run test:*` scripts). No Vitest runner.

## Commits

Follow [commit-conventions.mdc](commit-conventions.mdc) when the user asks to commit.
